  "verbalization": "Prephenic acid appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, (S)-3-phenyllactic acid, which in turn interacts with 60S ribosomal protein L26-like 1. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which involve the sequential targeting of prephenic acid, (S)-3-phenyllactic acid, and the ribosomal protein. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant interaction across different molecular targets, indicating a potential mechanistic link. The involvement of ribosomal proteins in these pathways implies that the interaction may be related to translational control or ribosome function. The recurring role of (S)-3-phenyllactic acid as a mediator underscores the importance of this compound in the pathway, potentially linking prephenic acid to ribosomal protein modification or function. The integrated evidence supports a mechanism where prephenic acid modulates the activity of (S)-3-phenyllactic acid, which then affects 60S ribosomal protein L26-like 1, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction with the ribosome. This suggests a plausible, biologically relevant mechanism that warrants further investigation.",
